===== Return to factory/stock firmware =====
  * To boot the Zyxel firmware from the secondary/backup ROM again, you must go into U-boot mode, just like the previous procedure [[:toh:zyxel:gs1900-8hp_v1#oem_installation_using_the_tftp_method]]:

  * [[:toh:zyxel:gs1900-8hp_v1#serial|Connect serial]], power up the switch, interrupt U-boot by hitting the space bar, and enable the network: 
<code>U-Boot Version: 2.0.0.60266 (Jul 17 2015 - 12:29:50)

CPU:   500MHz
DRAM:  128 MB
FLASH: 16 MB
Model: ZyXEL_GS1900_8HP
SN:    ASDFSDFGHNVB
MAC:   12:34:56:12:34:56 - BC:DE:FA:AB:CD:EF

Press SPACE to abort boot script:  0 </code>
  * Since the GS1900-8HP is a dual-partition device, it's quite easy to get back to stock firmware. OpenWrt can only boot off the first partition anyway (hardcoded in the DTS). To make sure we are booting from the secondary/backup partition, issue the following commands:
  * make sure ''bootpartition'' is set to ''1'' by issuing the following commands:
<code>setsys bootpartition 1
savesys</code>
  * You can now reboot the device or issue a ''boot'' command.

From this state, flashing (or "updating") the primary boot partition (0) to the Zyxel OEM stock/factory firmware is easily done from the GUI now.

  * To get back to the OpenWRT firmware, just follow the same procedure, but change the ''1'' to ''0'':
<code>setsys bootpartition 0
savesys</code>

